course: dictionary
lesson: 4539
title: Many meanings of heart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one to use. In «a racing heart, shaky hands», heart is the organ in your chest that pumps blood. The clues are racing and shaky, which are things a body does.
explain: In «...that his own heart was singing to him», heart means your feelings. Hearts cannot sing, so the clue is that the feelings are happy and proud. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Phrases work as a whole. «Don't lose heart» means don't lose courage, and «learn by heart» means learn from memory. Learn these phrases as chunks, not word by word.
fact: Heart has several meanings: an organ in the body, feelings or kindness, the centre of something, a shape or card suit, and courage.
fact: The heart is a muscle about the size of your fist, and it pumps blood around your body.
fact: At rest, a child's heart beats about 70 to 100 times a minute, and it beats faster when you run.
fact: «By heart» means from memory, so to learn something by heart means you can say it without reading.
fact: «Lose heart» means lose courage, or stop believing you can succeed.
exercise: «...a racing heart, shaky hands...» What does heart mean here? | The centre of a city | Kindness | *The organ in your chest that pumps blood | A playing card
exercise: «...that his own heart was singing to him». What does heart mean here? | The organ that pumps blood | A playing card | The middle of the road | *His feelings, joy and pride
exercise: «Don't lose heart.» What does this mean? | Don't drop your cards | *Don't lose courage | Don't leave the room | Don't lose your heartbeat
test: «Learn the poem by heart» means? | Very slowly and quietly | Out loud, in a loud voice | *From memory | Draw a red heart on it
test: «The heart of the city» means what? | A sad feeling | The organ that pumps blood | *The centre, the most important part | The shape of a valentine card
exam: Which fact is true? | A heart beats once a day | Your heart is in your foot | A child's heart is as big as a football | *A child's heart beats about 70 to 100 times a minute at rest
